<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Geronimo came in without an appointment, with the interpreter, for a cough for six days, at first dry and now with a little clear sputum, with aches and a low fever at night. Several people near his house have had the same cold. He has no chest pain, no shortness of breath at rest and no confusion. He started sertraline 25 mg two weeks ago and takes naltrexone daily. He has not drunk alcohol for the past week, he says, because he felt too ill. A friend offered him a cough syrup that contains alcohol and codeine, and he wanted to know whether it was safe. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Six days ago, after neighbors had colds</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Cough with a little clear sputum</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; tiring but able to work</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Aches and low fever at night; no chest pain, breathlessness at rest or confusion</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Naltrexone daily; sertraline 25 mg for two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Warm drinks help a little</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

