<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute bronchitis (J20.9)</content>. Acute bronchitis, almost always viral; the chest X-ray is clear and his oxygen and breathing rate are acceptable, so pneumonia is unlikely. CRB-65 score 1, for age only. Antibiotics do not help bronchitis. Cough syrups with codeine are blocked by naltrexone and not advised, syrups with alcohol work against his goals, and dextromethorphan is best avoided with sertraline. [S]<list><item>No antibiotic.</item><item>Honey in warm water, fluids and rest.</item><item>Acetaminophen as needed, no more than 2,000 mg a day for two weeks.</item><item>Return the same day, or call 988 or the clinic at any hour, for breathlessness, chest pain, confusion, fever above 38.5 °C or a cough lasting more than three weeks.</item><item>Influenza, pneumococcal and RSV vaccines at the wellness visit once he is well.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, moderate (F10.20)</content>. No alcohol for a week. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]<list><item>Continue naltrexone and thiamine.</item><item>Keep the wallet card about opioid pain medicines with him.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); The American Psychiatric Association Practice Guideline for the Pharmacological Treatment of Patients With Alcohol Use Disorder (2018); Outpatient Clinical Care for Adults (antibiotic use) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Phone call in two days through the interpreter. Eleven-week review in three weeks. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-23: eleven-week review: therapy progress, sertraline and sodium, drinking and falls. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
